{
  "_comment": [
    "THE LINKED PROTOCOLS FIXTURE the root's protocol-axis tests read (root/tests/linked_protocols.rs).",
    "Data, not code (ARCHITECT F-T): the protocol names, paths, headers and bodies the shipped build's",
    "linked declarations are held to live here, so the test source names no plane. The declarations",
    "themselves are read off the linked table the root installs (`crate::LINKED.protocols`).",
    "protocol_order: the operator-visible provider protocol list, in order (metric-family index and the",
    "  config refusal's `must be one of:` tail; the published 1.5.5 binary's order).",
    "streaming_content_types / array_stream_shim_keys / head_keys: the registry's folded sets.",
    "resolver: [path, [[header, value]...], [protocol, verb] or null] — detection then operation.",
    "body_resolver: [path, body, [protocol, verb]] — the operation needs the body.",
    "mandatory_header: [path, [[header, value]], protocol] — a mandatory header beats path ordering.",
    "residual: [path, protocol] — the headerless residual classifier.",
    "residual_live: [path, protocol] — the positive control that proves the residual fold is live.",
    "residual_none: paths that name no dialect (the paths other planes mount at among them)."
  ],
  "protocol_order": ["anthropic", "openai", "gemini", "bedrock", "responses", "cohere"],
  "streaming_content_types": ["application/vnd.amazon.eventstream", "text/event-stream"],
  "array_stream_shim_keys": ["__busbar_gemini_json_array"],
